    "updated_at": "2021-05-19T20:51:13Z",
    "body": "[Here is where we scroll for find-in-page in chrome](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/finder/text_finder.cc;l=114-125;drc=d006dd153d442217cdafa2df3143b9eba132cda0), all of the relevant scrolling options appear to be there.\r\n\r\nFor sequential focus navigation (I'm guessing this means when you press tab to focus the next focusable element?), it looks like we simply [call element.focus()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/focus_controller.cc;l=1145-1146;drc=5c0ae0e0be971540b37bec305e03ae4860703c37) rather than having a separate scroll. I can also see that calling element.focus() from script also scrolls the element into view, but I'm having a hard time seeing exactly where the scroll is done just by reading the code. I can dig into it some more if that's helpful.",
