    "body": "> (I'm guessing this means when you press tab to focus the next focusable element?)\r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n> it looks like we simply call element.focus() \r\n\r\nOK. The spec doesn't do this currently, but maybe it should (or rather, move the algorithm for `element.focus()` to its own algorithm that `element.focus()` can use and that sequential focus navigation etc can use).\r\n\r\n@emilio do you know how focus and scrolling when tabbing works in Gecko?",
